      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Duplicate post by OP: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/eacrash-report\n\nI am not convinced this is a bug, this may be a vulnerable driver (versions 25.20.15031.5004 and 25.20.15031.9002) with a critical remote code execution vulnerability rated 10.0 on the CVSS 3.1 base score scale. See [CVE-2019-5049](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2019-5049). Read more: https://blog.talosintelligence.com/vuln-spotlight-amd-radeon-ati-sept-19/\n\nIf that's the case, Easy Anti-Cheat is doing the right thing by blocking your vulnerable graphics driver version (especially if the VRChat client is launched with administrator privileges).\n\nNonetheless it's not triggered in VRChat's code, but by Easy Anti-Cheat. This Canny board is for bug reports about VRChat.\n\n(off-topic) The `\\\\?\\GLOBALROOT\\Device\\HarddiskVolume9\\Windows\\System32\\atiadlxx.dll` path not a web URL, but a DOS device path exposed to the Win32 layer on Windows with the object manager underneath. The details are not important to discuss here, but it's practically the same as `%WINDIR%\\System32\\atiadlxx.dll` or most commonly `C:\\Windows\\System32\\atidlxx.dll`, which when opened in a web browser would be the `file:///C:/Windows/System32/atiadlxx.dll` URL. I'm pointing this out to say your shown URL is invalid (in a web browser), and to tell you what the right URL would be in a web browser.\n\n@{6080307d6f5d3a18c97ea08b|full_name} VRChat Feedback (Canny) is not an appropriate venue for this discussion, if you have questions or want to bring up general discussion you can submit a new topic on the [VRChat Ask](https://ask.vrchat.com/) forums. For assistance with launching VRChat due to an issue with Easy Anti-Cheat (EAC) visit the VRChat Help Desk at https://help.vrchat.com/.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
